1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,624
Earth is 4.5 billion years old. This planet is under 1 million.

2
00:00:05,624 --> 00:00:11,248
Elias 2-24 b, the youngest planet ever found

3
00:00:11,248 --> 00:00:18,981
Younger than any known world

4
00:00:18,981 --> 00:00:24,605
The previous youngest planets are over 5 million years old

5
00:00:24,605 --> 00:00:30,229
Roughly Jupiter's mass; models give about 2 to 4

6
00:00:30,229 --> 00:00:35,853
About 450 light-years away

7
00:00:35,853 --> 00:00:41,477
Still embedded in its disk, about 55 au from its star

8
00:00:41,477 --> 00:00:49,210
In archival Keck data, by a Universidad Diego Portales team
